    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I’ve always felt a bit uneasy around mathematics, especially beyond basic algebra. My background in chemistry and biology gave me some practical exposure, but I never developed a deep love for it. I see math as a tool, not a subject I’m passionate about. It’s logical, but it doesn’t resonate with me like science or nature does.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Yes, especially when problems get complex or when I’m expected to solve them quickly. My neuroticism makes me overthink and second-guess myself. I often feel overwhelmed by abstract concepts or when I don’t have enough time to work through them. It’s not just math—it’s the fear of making a mistake, especially in real-life situations.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "I used a simple AI app to check my homework on basic equations. It was helpful for quick verification, but I found it too simplistic and didn’t explain the reasoning behind steps. I felt frustrated when it gave answers without showing the logic. It didn’t reduce my anxiety—it just made me feel more uncertain about what I was doing.",
